{"museum":"Q5093884","name":"Chesterwood","checked":"2026-11-05","source":"Chesterwood’s Guide to the Studio, Map of the Estate and website; Wikimedia Commons","onViewKnown":true,"note":"Chesterwood was the summer home and studio of Daniel Chester French, sculptor of the Lincoln Memorial’s seated Lincoln and the Concord Minute Man. It holds the largest collection of his work anywhere: about 500 sculptures, 23 oil paintings and 13 pastels by French. This guide lists every piece in the Studio, wall by wall, from Chesterwood’s own Guide to the Studio, plus the buildings, gardens and collection highlights from its website. The online collection is not public, so the Residence’s contents are not listed one by one. Open May 15 – October 31.","works":[{"id":"cw-the-barn-gallery-and-visitor-center","title":"The Barn Gallery and Visitor Center","artist":"Chesterwood","medium":"Historic place","url":"https://www.chesterwood.org/the-residence-and-studio","imageUrl":"data/chesterwood/images/cw-the-barn-gallery-and-visitor-center.jpg","onView":true,"gallery":"Barn Gallery","floor":"G"},{"id":"cw-the-woodshed-gallery","title":"The Woodshed Gallery","artist":"Chesterwood","medium":"Historic place","url":"https://www.chesterwood.org/the-residence-and-studio","onView":true,"gallery":"Woodshed Gallery","floor":"G"},{"id":"cw-standing-lincoln","title":"Standing Lincoln","artist":"Chesterwood","medium":"Historic place","url":"https://www.chesterwood.org/the-residence-and-studio","onView":true,"gallery":"Standing Lincoln","floor":"G"},{"id":"cw-the-residence-1901-by-henry-bacon","title":"The Residence (1901) by Henry Bacon","artist":"Chesterwood","medium":"Historic place","url":"https://www.chesterwood.org/the-residence-and-studio","imageUrl":"data/chesterwood/images/cw-the-residence-1901-by-henry-bacon.jpg","onView":true,"gallery":"Residence","floor":"G"},{"id":"cw-the-piazza","title":"The piazza","artist":"Chesterwood","medium":"Room","url":"https://www.chesterwood.org/the-residence-a